          "findings"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    },
    "fix": {
      "kind": "agent",
      "provider": "codex",
      "workspace_base": 0,
      "instruction": "Follow docs/development-flow.md and docs/review-guidelines.md. Work only in your assigned worktree. Do not delegate or spawn subagents. Do not invoke live agent tests, push, publish, comment/review on GitHub or merge remote state; explicit GitWeave System Actions handle publication. Never redeem usage-limit reset tickets, buy allowance, or switch models/providers to bypass limits. Stop and return blocked if an actual permission/capability limitation prevents completion; do not invent an unsupported workaround or weaken requirements. Ordinary code/test defects are fixable findings, not capability blockers. Keep project material in English. Use deterministic tests and preserve existing behavior outside the issue's explicit change. Do not alter other worktrees or the original checkout.\n\nFix all upstream review findings for Issue #48 without expanding scope. Add focused regressions and run relevant deterministic checks. Preserve prior completed functionality. Leave files for the runtime checkpoint. Return ready when complete or blocked for a capability limitation.",
      "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "status": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "ready",
              "blocked"
            ]
